aj.ref.kind.own = This page
aj.ref.kind.other = Another page
aj.ref.kind.comment = A comment
aj.ref.kind.spacedesc = Space description
aj.ref.kind.history = An older version
aj.ref.kind.spacelogo = The space logo

aj.page.found = {0} found
aj.page.prev = Previous
aj.page.next = Next
aj.refs.none = No reference was found.
aj.refs.more = and {0} more (not stored).

# --- filters -----------------------------------------------------------------

aj.filter.all = All
aj.filter.label = Status
aj.filter.badge = Flag
aj.filter.extension = Type
aj.filter.minsize = At least
aj.filter.perpage = Per page
aj.filter.name = Name contains

# --- duplicates --------------------------------------------------------------

aj.dup.none = No duplicate files were found.
aj.dup.exact = Confirmed
aj.dup.maybe = Candidate
aj.dup.note = "Candidate" means the scan compared file size and the first 64 KB, not the \
whole file. Switch to a full hash in Settings if you need certainty.

# --- settings ----------------------------------------------------------------

aj.set.oldversioncount = Old versions: version count
aj.set.oldversioncount.hint = Flag a file once it has this many versions.
aj.set.oldversionbytes = Old versions: total size (MB)
aj.set.oldversionbytes.hint = Or once its superseded versions add up to this.
aj.set.largebytes = Large file (MB)
aj.set.largebytes.hint = Applies to the current version on its own.
aj.set.staledays = Untouched (days)
aj.set.staledays.hint = How long without a change before a file counts as untouched.
aj.set.hashbudget = Hashing limit per scan (MB)
aj.set.hashbudget.hint = How much the scan may read from disk to compare file contents. \
0 means no limit. Candidates beyond the limit are reported as unchecked, not as "not \
duplicates".
aj.set.keepruns = Scans to keep
aj.set.keepruns.hint = Per-space totals are kept for this many scans so you can see a trend. \
Per-attachment rows are only ever kept for the newest finished scan.
aj.set.keepactiondays = Cleanup records to keep (days)
aj.set.keepactiondays.hint = Removing older versions cannot be undone, so the record of what \
  was removed is the only trace. Records older than this are deleted the next time a cleanup \
  runs. The minimum is 30 days: a window of a few days is a recent-activity list, not an \
  audit trail.
aj.set.scanhistory = Examine past page versions
aj.set.scanhistory.hint = Needed to separate "History only" from "Unreferenced". \
Off by default: it adds a query per page version and can make a scan several times \
longer.
aj.set.dupmode = Duplicate detection
aj.set.dupmode.quick = Size and first 64 KB (fast)
aj.set.dupmode.full = Full SHA-1 (certain, reads every candidate)
aj.set.dupmode.hint = The fast mode reports "candidates" and never claims certainty.
aj.set.saved = Saved. The next scan will use these values.
aj.set.note = Changing a threshold does not re-label anything on its own - the statuses and \
flags you see were decided by the last scan.

# --- help --------------------------------------------------------------------

aj.help.title = Attachment Janitor - Help
aj.help.contents = Contents

aj.help.what = What this screen is
aj.help.what.body = Confluence does not tell an administrator how much disk each space's \
attachments take, and it does not show old versions at all: re-upload a file thirty times and \
the page still shows one file while thirty sit on disk. This app measures both, and works out \
which attachments no page body references any more.
aj.help.what.readonly = It removes nothing except superseded versions of an attachment, \
and only through a preview you confirm. It never removes an attachment, never moves one, and \
never touches a page. That narrowness is deliberate, not \
an unfinished feature: the point is to give you the evidence before you decide, and a report \
you might accidentally destroy something with is a report you would hesitate to run.

aj.help.labels = Status: what breaks if you remove it
aj.help.labels.intro = Every attachment gets exactly one status, and the axis is always the \
same question - what breaks if this file goes away. How big it is, or whether it is \
duplicated, is a separate axis and lives in the flags below.
aj.help.col.label = Status
aj.help.col.condition = When it is given
aj.help.col.action = What to do
aj.help.labels.confusion = "Unreferenced" and "History only" are the two that must not be \
confused. Removing an unreferenced file changes nothing anyone can see. Removing a \
history-only file changes nothing today either - and then someone opens last quarter's \
version of the page and finds a broken image. The current page looks identical in both cases, \
which is one of the reasons this app exists.
aj.help.labels.notrash = There is no "in the trash" status. When a page goes to the trash \
Confluence marks its attachments deleted, and the API this report reads does not return \
deleted attachments at all - so the status could never appear. A status that can never appear \
would read as "we checked and there are none", which would not be true.

aj.help.badges = Flags: how much it costs you
aj.help.badges.intro = Flags are independent of status and an attachment can carry several. \
A file can be in use and have twenty old versions; it can be unreferenced and duplicated. The \
thresholds below are your current settings, not fixed values.
aj.help.col.badge = Flag
aj.help.col.threshold = Current threshold
aj.help.col.meaning = What it means
aj.help.badges.settings = Change any of these in
aj.help.threshold.oldversions = {0} versions, or {1} MB of superseded versions
aj.help.threshold.large = {0} MB or more
aj.help.threshold.stale = No change for {0} days
aj.help.threshold.duplicate.quick = Size and first 64 KB match
aj.help.threshold.duplicate.full = Full SHA-1 match

aj.help.refs = Where a reference can come from
aj.help.refs.intro = Open the "Used by" count on any row to see the actual pages. A status \
whose evidence you cannot check is a status you should not act on, so every judgement here \
can be expanded.
aj.help.ref.desc.own = The current body of the page the file is attached to.
aj.help.ref.desc.other = The current body of some other page or blog post, including pages in \
other spaces. This is what makes an attachment risky to remove.
aj.help.ref.desc.comment = A comment. A comment on the file's own page counts as ordinary \
use; a comment on a different page counts as use from elsewhere.
aj.help.ref.desc.spacedesc = A space description. These are written in wiki markup rather \
than storage format, so they are read separately.
aj.help.ref.desc.history = A past version of a page body. Only collected when past versions \
are examined in Settings.
aj.help.ref.desc.spacelogo = The logo configured for the space. This one is not found in any \
body - a logo is an attachment on the space itself and nothing links to it. Without it the \
report would call every space logo unreferenced, when removing one visibly breaks the space \
header. Other files attached to the space that are not the logo stay unreferenced, because \
they really are unused.

aj.help.duplicates = Duplicates
aj.help.duplicates.body = Finding duplicates in two stages keeps it cheap. Files are first \
grouped by exact size and extension - files of different sizes cannot have the same content, \
so this stage misses nothing and most files drop out of it alone. Only what survives is read \
from disk and hashed.
aj.help.duplicates.mode = In the default fast mode the scan reads a file's size and its first \
64 KB, which is a strong hint but not a proof, so those groups are labelled "Candidate". \
Switch to a full hash in Settings when you want certainty; it reads every candidate file end \
to end.

aj.help.limits = What this report cannot tell you
aj.help.duplicates.columns = The columns on that screen mean this:
aj.help.limit.notdelete = The only change it can make is removing superseded versions of an \
attachment, through the preview described above. Removing an attachment itself, or moving \
one, is still done in Confluence.
aj.help.limit.sizes = Sizes are the attachment files as Confluence records them. Search \
indexes, thumbnails and extracted text are not included, so the total is smaller than the \
home directory.
aj.help.limit.deleted = Attachments Confluence has already marked deleted - a trashed page, \
or an attachment deleted on its own - keep their files on disk but are not counted here, \
because the API this report reads does not return them.
aj.help.limit.history = With past versions switched off, an attachment used only by an older \
version of a page is reported as unreferenced and marked "history not checked".
aj.help.limit.templates = Page templates and blueprints are not read. An attachment used only \
by a template will be reported as unreferenced.
aj.help.limit.external = "Unreferenced" means no reference was found in the places this app \
looks. A macro it cannot parse, an external system linking straight to the download URL, or a \
page body it failed to read all produce the same answer. Treat it as the first place to look, \
not as permission to delete.
aj.help.limit.snapshot = Everything on these screens comes from the last scan, and the time \
it was taken is shown next to the buttons. Nothing is measured when you open the page.
aj.help.limit.oneatatime = Only one job runs at a time: a scan and a cleanup exclude each \
other, and on Data Center that holds across the whole cluster. A request that arrives while \
another job is running is refused rather than queued. Progress is visible, and Cancel works, \
only on the node running the job.

# --- 구버전 정리 (되돌릴 수 없는 유일한 기능) ---
aj.clean.pickall = Select every file that has older versions
aj.clean.picked = {0} selected, {1} older versions would go
aj.clean.keep = Keep last
aj.clean.keepnote = Counting the current version. Older versions beyond that are removed - \
the file itself is never removed, whatever its status says, so no page can break.
aj.clean.preview = Preview removal
aj.clean.confirmtitle = Remove older versions
aj.clean.summary = {0} files, {1} older versions, {2} reclaimed. The most recent {3} versions \
of each file are kept, including the current one.
aj.clean.irreversible = This cannot be undone. Confluence has no trash for attachment \
versions - the rows and the files are removed immediately. Pages are not affected: the \
current version stays and page bodies reference attachments by name, never by version.
aj.clean.problems = {0} of the selected files could not be read and are not included.
aj.clean.current = Current
aj.clean.removing = Removing
aj.clean.reclaim = Reclaimed
aj.clean.versions = Version numbers
aj.clean.execute = Remove them
aj.clean.cancel = Cancel
aj.clean.running = Removing older versions...
aj.clean.done = Removed {1} older versions from {0} files, reclaiming {2}. Run a scan to \
refresh the numbers.
aj.clean.partial = {0} files were skipped because they changed since the preview, and {1} \
failed.
aj.clean.nothing = Nothing to remove for the files you selected.
aj.clean.previewing = Reading versions... {0} of {1} files.
aj.clean.previewstopped = The preview stopped partway. Nothing has been removed. Try again.
aj.clean.preparing = Working out what to remove...
aj.clean.progress = Removing... {0} of {1} files, {2} reclaimed so far.
aj.clean.stop = Stop
aj.clean.cancelled = Stopped partway. Versions already removed are gone for good.
aj.clean.failed = The cleanup could not finish ({0}). Versions already removed are gone for good.
aj.clean.startfailed = The cleanup could not be started. Nothing has been removed.
aj.clean.toomany = At most {0} files can be removed in one go; {1} are selected. Narrow the \
  filter or clear some of the selection.
aj.clean.keepchanged = "Keep last" was changed while the preview was being read, so that \
  preview was discarded. Press Preview again.
aj.clean.superseded = Your run has finished, and another run has started since. The table \
  has been reloaded; run a scan for exact numbers.
aj.clean.detached = Lost contact with the server while following the cleanup. It may still be \
  running there. This screen will try to reconnect; reload it to be sure.
aj.clean.keepslow = Removal runs in the background on the server. You can close this page - \
  it keeps going, and this screen picks it up again when you come back.

# --- 설명서: 구버전 정리 ---
aj.help.cleanup = Removing older versions
aj.help.cleanup.why = This is the one thing the app can remove, and the reason it exists is \
simple: a list of files you cannot act on does not free any storage. On the test \
instance 1,048 superseded versions sat behind 12 filenames - nothing on any page pointed at \
them, and no screen in Confluence shows you where they are.
aj.help.cleanup.safe = Removing an older version cannot break a page, and that is a property \
of the storage format rather than a hope. A page body refers to an attachment by file name and \
container; there is no field in which it could name a version. So the current version always \
answers, whatever the status of the file says. This is why the status - In use, Used \
elsewhere, Unreferenced - has no bearing on whether removing older versions is safe, and why \
the app does not hide the checkbox based on it.
aj.help.cleanup.keep = "Keep last N" counts the current version. A file with sixteen versions \
and N of 3 keeps the current one plus the two most recent older ones, and loses thirteen. N \
does not change what breaks - nothing does - it decides how far back you can still roll the \
file. The default of 3 reclaims almost everything while leaving two steps of undo.
aj.help.cleanup.flow = The flow is fixed and there is no way around it:
aj.help.cleanup.rule.oldonly = A checkbox appears only on files that the current \
"keep last" value would actually take versions from. Files with nothing to remove get \
no control at all, so a button is never enabled on something that would do nothing.
aj.help.cleanup.rule.nolabel = Status is never used to hide the checkbox. Hiding it by status \
would teach a rule that does not exist and would be wrong the first time someone relied on it.
aj.help.cleanup.rule.preview = Nothing is removed without a preview. The preview is read live \
at that moment, not taken from the last scan, so it can disagree with the table - and when it \
does, the preview is the one that is right.
aj.help.cleanup.rule.recheck = At the moment of removal each file is read once more and \
compared with what the preview showed you. If someone uploaded or removed a version in \
between, that one file is skipped and reported; the rest go ahead.
aj.help.cleanup.rule.background = Removal runs on the server, not in your browser. The page \
hands the work over and then follows its progress, so a large batch cannot be cut short by a \
proxy or load balancer closing an idle connection. You can close the page and come back: the \
work keeps going and this screen picks it up again. Stop halts it before the next file - \
versions already removed are not restored.
aj.help.cleanup.rule.log = Every file is recorded - what was removed, by whom, when, and the \
version numbers - and each run also gets a one-line summary so a large batch does not bury \
the runs before it. Skipped and failed files are recorded too, because a silent omission is \
the worst outcome. Records are kept for the number of days set on the Settings screen, a \
year by default, and are deleted the next time a cleanup runs.
aj.help.cleanup.rule.websudo = Removal asks for your password again even though reading does \
not. A few seconds is worth it in front of something irreversible. Stop is the exception: it \
never asks, because an expired confirmation must not leave you unable to halt a running \
removal.
aj.help.cleanup.caveat = Two things to know before you use it. It cannot be undone: Confluence \
has no trash for attachment versions, so the database rows and the files on disk go \
immediately. And if anyone has linked directly to a download URL with a version pinned in it, \
that link breaks - the app does not follow URLs, so it cannot warn you about those.

# --- 스페이스 막대 (색에 이름을 붙인다) ---
aj.bar.latest = Current versions
aj.bar.old = Older versions
aj.bar.rest = Remaining space up to the largest space
aj.bar.title = Current versions {0}, older versions {1}. The full width is {2}, the largest \
space here.

# --- 설명서: 스페이스 막대 ---
aj.help.bar = Reading the bar next to each space
aj.help.bar.body = Each space name has a thin bar under it. It is drawn to scale against the \
largest space in the table, so the widest bar is the space using the most attachment storage \
and every other bar is a fraction of it. The bar is not a percentage of your disk.
aj.help.bar.colours = The bar carries three colours, and the split is the point of it:
aj.help.bar.latest = Blue is what the current versions of the files occupy. This is the part \
you would still be storing if every file had only ever been uploaded once.
aj.help.bar.old = Amber is what superseded versions occupy. Confluence shows none of this \
anywhere: the page lists one file, and the older copies sit on disk behind it. A space that is \
mostly amber is a space where the storage is going into history rather than content, and that \
is exactly what the clean-up action can reclaim.
aj.help.bar.rest = Grey is simply the rest of the bar - the distance up to the largest space. \
It means nothing about the space itself.

# --- 칸 이름만으로는 뜻이 안 통하는 칸의 설명 (표 머리에 ? 로 뜬다) ---
aj.col.dupfiles.tip = How many files in this group hold the same content.
aj.col.unit.tip = The size of one of them. They are all the same size - that is how the \
group was formed.
aj.col.reclaim.tip = What you would get back by keeping one copy and removing the rest. It \
is the size of one file times the number of extra copies. This app does not remove them; the \
number is here so you can judge whether it is worth doing in Confluence.
aj.col.certainty.tip = Whether the contents were compared in full. "Confirmed" means every \
byte matched. "Candidate" means only the size and the first 64 KB matched, which is the \
default because reading every file costs disk I/O. Switch to full comparison in Settings.
aj.col.risky.tip = Attachments referenced from somewhere other than the page they are \
attached to. Removing one of these breaks a page that is not the obvious one, so open the \
evidence before touching them.
aj.col.versions.tip = The number the current version carries. Deleted version numbers are \
never reissued, so after a cleanup this can be larger than the old-version count plus one.
aj.col.oldversions.tip = Two numbers: the storage held by superseded versions, then how \
many of those versions are still on disk. They are the copies hidden behind a single file \
name, and Confluence shows neither number anywhere.
aj.col.orphans.tip = Attachments that no page body references, as far as this app can see. \
The cell shows their total size, then how many of them there are. Read the limits before \
treating this as "safe to delete".

# --- 체크박스가 무엇에 대한 것인지 (상태와 무관하다는 것이 핵심) ---
aj.col.pick.tip = Select files whose older versions you want removed. This never removes \
the file itself, so the Status column has no bearing on it: the current version stays and \
page bodies reference attachments by name, never by version. Files that the current \
"keep last" value would take nothing from have no checkbox, because there is nothing \
to remove.
aj.clean.picktip = Select this file: {0} older versions would be removed, the current version \
stays.
